it\nBTC/USDT\n54.81万\n$7.81万\n24.99亿\n0.9%\n36\nCrypto.com\nBTC/USDT\n53.19万\n$7.81万\n21.46亿\n0.77%\n37\nSlex\nBTC/USDT\n80.63万\n$7.81万\n20.08亿\n0.72%\n38\nD网\nBTC/USDT\n60.41万\n$7.81万\n19.93亿\n0.72%\n39\n火币\nBTC/USDT\n52.26万\n$7.81万\n18.65亿\n0.67%\n40\nBitrue\nBTC/USDT\n53.30万\n$7.81万\n18.15亿\n0.65%\n41\n库币网\nBTC/USDT\n币种介绍\n比特币(英文BitCoin，简称BTC，货币符号฿)的概念最初由中本聪在2009年提出，目前是上线最多交易所的数字货币，比特币根据中本聪的思路设计发布的开源软件以及建构其上的P2P网络。比特币是一种P2P形式的数字货币。点对点的传输意味着一个去中心化的支付系统。\n与大多数货币不同，比特币不依靠特定货币机构发行，它依据特定算法，通过大量的计算产生，比特币经济使用整个P2P网络中众多节点构成的分布式数据库来确认并记录所有的交易行为，并使用密码学的设计来确保货币流通各个环节安全性。P2P的去中心化特性与算法本身可以确保无法通过大量制造比特币来人为操控币值。\n基于密码学的设计可以使比特币只能被真实的拥有者转移或支付。这同样确保了货币所有权与流通交易的匿名性。比特币与其他虚拟货币最大的不同，是其总数量非常有限，具有极强的稀缺性。该货币系统曾在4年内只有不超过1050万个，之后的总数量将被永久限制在2100万个。\n比特币可以用来兑现，可以兑换成大多数国家的货币。使用者可以用比特币购买一些虚拟物品，比如网络游戏当中的衣服、帽子、装备等，只要有人接受，也可以使用比特币购买现实生活当中的物品。\n比特币和区块链关系\n区块链是比特币架构的核心，充当去中心化和不可篡改的账本，这个公开账本记录了网络上的每一笔交易，这些交易被组织成一个个加密相互链接的区块。\n每个区块包含已验证的交易列表、时间戳以及对前一个区块的引用，形成一个连续的链条。区块链的设计确保了透明性并防止篡改，因为更改一个区块需要修改所有后续区块，并获得对网络的多数控制。这一特性是比特币信任机制的关键因素。\n区块链通过共识机制来验证交易并确保网络完整性。在比特币中，这一机制被称为工作量证明(PoW)，矿工通过解决复杂的数学难题来竞争。第一个成功解决难题的矿工将新增区块添加到区块链并获得奖励。这个过程需要大量的计算资源，使恶意行为者难以破坏网络\nBTC工作量证明机制\nBTC 采用了PoW，即工作量证明的共识机制来保证区块链的一致性以及防篡改特性。也正是因为基于 PoW 的机制，才会衍生出 BTC 挖矿所涉及到的数学计算问题，即我们所熟知的算力。PoW 为参与 BTC 的网络在节点上提供相应的问题，人们通过计算机设备所产生的算力参与问题的解答，这个过程便被称之为“挖矿”。\nBTC 网络对参与节点的矿工的激励模式，每次交易都会被记录在全网的各个节点中，最早计算出 PoW 所提供的问题答案的节点就拥有了首次记账权，可以获得 BTC 形式的区块奖励。\n挖矿可以获取一定收益，通常情况下矿工挖矿的过程就是通过运行BTC 节点，同步历史账本，将最新交易记录到账本内，并获得 BTC 区块奖励的一个过程。支撑这个过程的基础便是 PoW 机制，由于 BTC 对整个加密市场的影响，PoW 机制也成为了各类主流币种的共识机制之一。\nBTC比特币减半机制\n中本聪在设计BTC时，便为这套体系加入了一个抑制机制——减半机制。\n根据 BTC 的设计，每 10 分钟可以产生一个交易记录块。最初每生产一个交易记录块，会有 50 个 BTC 的奖励，因此最初每天会有 7200 个 BTC 产生，但每 4 年会减半，最终系统中只能有2100万个，直到节点奖励完毕。\n当然这不是说这套机制对于参与挖矿的节点矿工们来说是多么有益。相反，BTC 每 4 年一次的减半机制对从业者和市场的影响非常大。\n自 BTC诞生至今，它的减半机制已经生效了三次，分别是 2012年11月、2016 年7月、 2020年5月以及2024年4月。\nBTC比特币创始人介绍\n比特币的发明人是化名中本聪(Satoshi Nakamoto)的一个人或者一个团队。在2008年，中本聪发表了比特币的白皮书，并在2009年正式启动了比特币网络。虽然他的真实身份到现在仍然是一个谜，但他的创造已经彻底改变了全球金融和技术的格局。\n在2010年之后，中本聪逐渐退出了公众视野，之后比特币的社区和开发者团队接管了比特币项目的发展。这种「无中心领导」的模式，加强了比特币去中心化的特性，令它不受单一机构或者个人控制。\n中本聪的神秘身份引起了很多猜测，但无论他是谁，比特币的出现已经深远影响了全球经济和技术创新，成为现代金融科技发展的重要里程碑。\nBTC比特币优点汇总\n1、去中心化：比特币是第一种分布式虚拟货币，整个网络由用户构成，没有中央银行。去中心化是其安全与自由的保证 。\n2、全世界流通：可以在任意一台接入互联网的电脑上管理。不管身处何方，任何人都可以挖掘、购买、出售或收取比特币。\n3、专属所有权：操控比特币需要私钥，它可以被隔离保存在任何存储介质。除了用户自己之外无人可以获取。\n4、低交易费用：可以免费汇出比特币，但最终对每笔交易将收取约1比特分的交易费以确保交易更快执行。\n5、无隐藏成本：作为由A到B的支付手段，比特币没有繁琐的额度与手续限制。知道对方比特币地址就可以进行支付。\n6、跨平台挖掘：用户可以在众多平台上发掘不同硬件的计算能力。\nBTC比特币的价值和意义\n1.固定供应和稀缺性\n与可以无限期印刷的法定货币不同，比特币的硬上限为 2100 万枚，从而产生了内在的稀缺性,已经开采了超过 1900 万枚 BTC，使剩余的供应更有价值。\n2.去中心化和安全\n比特币在没有中央权威的情况下运行，降低了政府控制和通货膨胀的风险,其强大的加密安全性可防止黑客攻击和双重支付。\n3.对冲通胀\n随着政府印发更多货币，法定货币会随着时间的推移而贬值,比特币具有固定供应量和去中心化的特性，通常被视为对冲通胀的工具。\n4.机构采用\n大型公司、对冲基金和金融机构投资比特币，提高了其市场信誉。萨尔瓦多等国家已将比特币作为法定货币，加强了其在全球金融体系中的作用。\n比特币价值储存概念\n比特币是首个去中心化的点对点数字货币。其最重要的功能之一是作为一种去中心化的价值储存手段。换句话说，它既可以作为实物资产，也可以作为记账单位，赋予所有权。然而，后者的价值储存功能一直备受争议。许多加密货币爱好者和经济学家认为，这种顶级货币的大规模采用将引领我们进入一个全新的现代金融世界，届时交易金额将以更小的单位计价。\n比特币的最小单位是0.00000001BTC，被称为(Satoshis，简称Sats)，以此向这位匿名的创造者致敬。以比特币目前的汇率计算，1聪约合0.00048美元。\n对许多人来说，顶级加密货币被视为一种价值储存手段，就像黄金一样，而非一种货币。将顶级加密货币视为一种价值储存手段而非支付手段，意味着许多人会购买加密货币并长期持有(或HODL)，而不是像通常花美元那样将其用于购买物品——将其视为数字黄金。\n比特币 ETF是什么？\n美国证券交易委员会(SEC)于美国时间2024 年1 月批准了首批比特币现货ETF，比特币 ETF(Bitcoin Exchange Traded Fund)是一种追踪比特币价格的交易型基金，可以像股票一样在传统交易所买卖，它的设计目的，是让投资人可以不需要直接持有或管理比特币，也能享受与比特币价格表现一致的投资收益。比特币 ETF 可分为两种：\n现货比特币 ETF(Spot ETF)：直接购买并持有实体比特币，价格最贴近市场\n比特币期货 ETF(Futures ETF)：透过 CME 等期货市场合约追踪比特币走势，并非实体持币\n目前交易量最大的比特币ETF 包括贝莱德(BlackRock)的IBIT、灰度(Grayscale)的GBTC，以及富达投资(Fidelity)的FBTC。美国的比特币ETF 市场规模高于香港。\n台湾尚未开放比特币ETF 的本土发行，但台湾投资者可以透过美国券商或香港券商开设海外交易账户，购买境外上市的比特币ETF。此外，金管会已允许专业投资人透过复委托方式参与投资。\n基本信息\n发行时间\n2009-01-03\n发行价格\n$0.0025\n众筹价格\n$0.0025\n历史最高\n¥85.84万\n历史最低\n¥461.65\n上架交易所\n319家\n发行总量\n2100.00万\n流通总量\n2003.04万\n流通市值\n10.64万亿\n流通率\n95.38%\n市值占比\n54.91%\n基础链\nBitcoin\n核心算法\nSHA-256\n共识机制\nPoW\n区块时间\n10分钟\n区块奖励\n3.125BTC\n挖矿方式\nCPU/GPU\n概念板块\nPoW /  GMCI指数 /  Coinbase50指数 /  智能合约 /  Layer1(L1) /  FTX Holdings /  比特币生态 /  GMCI 30指数\n","publishTime":"2026-05-17T09:16:37+08:00"},{"title":"通胀暴击，比特币暴跌？","url":"https://c.m.163.com/news/a/KT6EN1I105199N88.html","siteName":"网易新闻客户端","snippet":"通胀暴击，比特币暴跌？\n澳洲财经见闻\n2026-05-18 04:34·上海·优质财经领域创作者\n1\n通\n胀回升压制降息预期，导致比特币阶段性承压\n据BIT分析，若比特币能够跟上纳斯达克的涨势，当前价格本应接近\n14万美元。比特币的相对跑输，可能与2025年三季度以来通胀重新抬头有关。整体来看，比特币此前大体跟随纳\n斯达克波动，但自2025年10月起，两者之间的分化开始明显扩大。\n当时，最新的CPI读数已回升至3.0% \n本文作者：澳洲财经见闻","content":"通胀暴击，比特币暴跌？\n澳洲财经见闻\n2026-05-18 04:34·上海·优质财经领域创作者\n1\n通胀回升压制降息预期，导致比特币阶段性承压\n据BIT分析，若比特币能够跟上纳斯达克的涨势，当前价格本应接近14万美元。比特币的相对跑输，可能与2025年三季度以来通胀重新抬头有关。整体来看，比特币此前大体跟随纳斯达克波动，但自2025年10月起，两者之间的分化开始明显扩大。\n当时，最新的CPI读数已回升至3.0%，较美联储目标高出100个基点，利率市场也开始逐步撤回对2026年降息的部分定价。而这恰恰是比特币真正承压的源头，比特币的上涨逻辑依赖美联储宽松预期，一旦市场对降息的定价开始回撤，表现往往随之承压。此后，这一逻辑持续影响比特币走势。股票则截然不同。只要市场仍将通胀视为温和、阶段性的，通胀回升反而对股票有利：即使销量未明显增长，也能推高企业名义收入、降低实际债务负担，并增强股票作为购买力对冲的吸引力。\n最新公布的美国通胀数据似乎令部分市场参与者措手不及，尽管该机构的模型此前已提示价格压力可能再度回升。当前的关键问题在于：这轮通胀预期的重新定价，是否会削弱比特币持续向好的基本面；以及在这一背景下，投资者接下来应如何调整仓位。\n2\n泰国突击搜查一处非法比特币挖矿窝点，电力损失超8万美元\n据 Khaosod English 报道，泰国当局突查一处涉嫌非法比特币挖矿场所。由于异常高耗电导致周边建筑电缆过热熔化，执法人员对一栋四层商业楼展开突击搜查。调查发现，该场所涉嫌非法接入主电网，为四楼多台比特币矿机供电，造成电力损失预估超 8 万美元，而其登记月电费仅约 11 美元。目前，警方已查获相关挖矿设备，并正对涉案人员展开进一步调查。\n3\nYZi Labs领投AI教育平台VideoTutor 1100万美元种子轮融资\nYZi Labs 在 X 平台表示，已领投 AI 教育平台 VideoTutor 的 1100 万美元种子轮融资，并支持其完成产品上线。VideoTutor 表示，其 AI 产品可能监控、教学，并为每位学生打造独特的学习体验。\n4\n马斯克回应Grok模型更新进展缓慢：V9刚完成训练，预计3至4周后发布\n针对“Grok 模型进展缓慢”的提问，马斯克在 X 平台回应称，“我们正在对 0.5T Grok 基础模型 V8（公开版本 4.3）进行持续改进，每隔几天就会更新一次。1.5T V9 模型刚刚完成训练，这是一次重大升级。接下来，我们将添加 Cursor 数据进行补充训练，然后进行 SFT 和 RL 训练。预计 3 到 4 周后发布。”\n5\nDACC完成1000万美元战略融资，复星国际等参投\n据Aastocks报道，代币化金融市场基础设施Digital Asset Clearing Center（DACC）宣布完成1000万美元战略融资，Conflux、卓信科技Global InfoTech、复星国际、Blockstone、Avior Capital、Fintech World、Satoshi Ventures及BridgeTower等参投，DACC目前为金融机构提供端到端的“清算即服务”（Clearing-as-a-Service），新资金将支持其构建合规金融结算及清算基础设施。\n17\n16\n \n本文作者：澳洲财经见闻","publishTime":"2026-05-18T04:34:00+08:00"},{"title":"ETF异动 | 比特币ETF跌幅居前 市场担忧各国央行维持紧缩政策 比特币跌穿7.7万美元","url":"http://m.163.com/dy/article/KT762BHB05198UNI.html","siteName":"网易","snippet":"央行维持紧缩政策 比特币跌穿7.7万美元\n智通财经\n2026-05-18 11:22\n智通财经APP获悉，比特币ETF跌幅居前，截至发稿\n策略师表示，全球债券市场 正在遭遇抛售，推动利率上升，同时加剧了包括加密货币在内的高风险资产避险情绪。\n值得注意的是，近期，多家头部加密\n构第一季度的业绩均出现大幅下滑。根据Strategy官方财报，该公司2026年一季度净亏损达125.4亿美元。Strategy CEO  \n本文作者：智通财经","content":"ETF异动 | 比特币ETF跌幅居前 市场担忧各国央行维持紧缩政策 比特币跌穿7.7万美元\n智通财经\n2026-05-18 11:22\n智通财经APP获悉，比特币ETF跌幅居前，截至发稿，华夏SOL(03460)跌6.91%，报3.424港元；嘉实以太币(03179)跌6.44%，报4.996港元；博时比特币(03008)跌5%，报5.895港元；华夏比特币(03042)跌4.88%，报9.355港元。\n消息面上，周一，比特币跌破77000美元。随着美国与伊朗冲突持续升级，投资者担忧全球通胀压力可能进一步加剧，并迫使各国央行维持更长时间的紧缩政策。JonesTrading首席市场策略师表示，全球债券市场 正在遭遇抛售，推动利率上升，同时加剧了包括加密货币在内的高风险资产避险情绪。\n值得注意的是，近期，多家头部加密企业相继发布财报，Coinbase、Strategy、Bakkt等知名机构第一季度的业绩均出现大幅下滑。根据Strategy官方财报，该公司2026年一季度净亏损达125.4亿美元。Strategy CEO 在财报电话会议上表示，称公司可能出售部分比特币来支付股息。\n \n本文作者：智通财经","publishTime":"2026-05-18T11:22:00+08:00"},{"title":"Bitcoin Price Dips To Around $81,000 On May 11, 2026 Amid Market Volatility And Prediction Market Shifts","url":"https://infointeract.com/bitcoin-price-dips-to-around-81000-on-may-11-2026-amid-market-volatility-and-prediction-market-shifts/","siteName":"Info Interact","snippet":"shot\nAs of 6:06 PM UTC, Bitcoin’s price hovered near $81,037 on Coin\ngures: bitFlyer listed BTC at $81,187, up 0.60% intraday but within \nBitcoin’s price action on May 11, 2026, showing intraday volatility.","content":"Bitcoin Price Dips To Around $81,000 On May 11, 2026 Amid Market Volatility And Prediction Market Shifts\nEditor\nCrypto\nTable of Contents\nBitcoin Price Dips to Around $81,000 on May 11, 2026 Amid Market Volatility and Prediction Market Shifts\nBitcoin Price Dips to Around $81,000 on May 11, 2026 Amid Market Volatility and Prediction Market Shifts\nBy Crypto News Desk | May 11, 2026\nBitcoin (BTC) traded around $81,000 on Monday, May 11, 2026, marking a modest decline from recent highs as cryptocurrency markets grapple with ongoing volatility. Live data from major exchanges showed prices fluctuating between $80,500 and $82,300, reflecting a approximately 1-3% drop over the past 24 hours amid broader market uncertainty.\nCurrent Market Snapshot\nAs of 6:06 PM UTC, Bitcoin’s price hovered near $81,037 on Coinbase, down 3.04% from $91,151 recorded earlier in the day and a steeper 13% retreat from $104,388 a week prior. Other platforms reported similar figures: bitFlyer listed BTC at $81,187, up 0.60% intraday but within a 24-hour range of $80,345 to $82,347. Investing.com pegged the latest close at $80,994, following a -1.40% change on May 11.\nDiscrepancies across exchanges highlighted liquidity variations, with Coinbase emphasizing a current value of $91,151 amid intraday swings—though real-time trackers confirmed the sub-$82,000 consensus. Bitcoin’s market capitalization stood at approximately $1.62 trillion on bitFlyer, underscoring its dominance in a $3 trillion-plus crypto ecosystem.\nBitcoin’s price action on May 11, 2026, showing intraday volatility. Source: Aggregated exchange data.\nPrediction Markets Signal Confidence Above Key Thresholds\nPrediction markets provided a bullish undertone despite the dip. On Polymarket, the market for “Bitcoin above ___ on May 11?” overwhelmingly favored “above $70,000” at 100% probability, with $2.48 million in volume. The event, tied to Binance BTC/USDT pricing and set to resolve today, saw negligible bets on lower tiers, signaling trader consensus that BTC comfortably cleared the $70K mark.\nRobinhood’s prediction contracts echoed this, with strong positioning for “$71,100 or above” at the 2 AM EDT snapshot (6 AM UTC). These markets, which opened May 4, reflect speculative fervor even as spot prices cooled from April peaks.\nWeekly Trends and Historical Context\nOver the past seven days, Bitcoin shed about 12-13%, per Revolut and Coinbase data, after failing to sustain momentum post its all-time high of $126,210 on October 6, 2025—a 28% drawdown from that pinnacle. Recent historical data from Investing.com showed May 11 opening at $81,036, peaking at $82,288 before settling lower, with volume at 47.58K units.\nPreceding days painted a volatile picture: May 10 closed with a -0.50% change amid $81K volume, while May 9 saw +2.42%. This week’s trajectory follows a broader correction from $120K+ levels in early May, as noted in bitbo.io’s long-term charts showing $118,838 as a fleeting high.\n“Bitcoin’s resilience above $80K amid macro headwinds speaks to institutional accumulation, but short-term sellers are capping upside.”\n— Anonymous market analyst, via crypto forums\nFactors Influencing the Dip\nSeveral elements contributed to today’s softening. Heightened geopolitical tensions and U.S. regulatory scrutiny on crypto ETFs weighed on sentiment, while profit-taking followed last week’s rally. Revolut noted a 24-hour trading volume of £67.6 billion (~$85 billion USD), with BTC/USD up 0.62% in GBP terms but down in USD aggregates.\nTechnical indicators pointed to support near $80,000, with resistance at $85,000. On-chain metrics, including whale movements, suggested accumulation by long-term holders, potentially setting the stage for a rebound if macro conditions stabilize.\nBroader Market Implications\nBitcoin’s movement rippled across altcoins, with Ethereum and others mirroring the 1-2% decline. Institutional interest remains robust, evidenced by record ETF inflows earlier in 2026, though retail caution prevailed today.\nAnalysts eye upcoming events, including potential Federal Reserve signals and Bitcoin halving aftereffects, as catalysts. Polymarket’s 100% on $70K+ underscores baseline optimism, but traders warn of flash crashes if $80K support breaks.\nLooking Ahead\nAs May 11 closes, all eyes are on evening UTC trading. A close above $81,500 could signal bullish reversal, while sub-$80K might accelerate selling. With prediction markets resolved soon, fresh bets on June targets could inject liquidity.\nInvestors are advised to monitor exchange-specific data, as variances persist. Bitcoin’s journey from sub-$100K in early 2026 to today’s levels reaffirms its volatility-driven narrative.\nKey Stats at a Glance\nPrice: ~$81,000 USD\n24h Change: -1% to -3%\n7d Change: -12-13%\nMarket Cap: $1.62T\nATH: $126,210 (Oct 6, 2025)\nThis article aggregates real-time data from Coinbase, Polymarket, bitFlyer, Investing.com, and others. Crypto prices are highly volatile; past performance is not indicative of future results. Always conduct your own research.\n","publishTime":"2026-05-12T00:07:00+08:00"},{"title":"2026年比特币价格实时查询：今日美元与人民币行情及K线走势解读","url":"https://www.tijian8.com/post/3dF1F0481A80.html","siteName":"善检网","snippet":"2026年比特币价格实时查询：今日美元与人民币行情及K线走势解读\nguodiaoan\n2026-05-16 16:33:09\n对于许多关\n注数字资产的朋友来说，每日查看比特币的价格动态，就像查看天气一样，已成为一种习惯。尤其是在市场波动加剧的时期，掌握实时、准确的价格信息，\n对于做出判断至关重要。今天，我们就来聚焦2026年的比特币市场，为大家提供一份详尽的今日价格查询指南，并解读背后的关键信息。\n一、202","content":"2026年比特币价格实时查询：今日美元与人民币行情及K线走势解读\nguodiaoan\n2026-05-16 16:33:09\n对于许多关注数字资产的朋友来说，每日查看比特币的价格动态，就像查看天气一样，已成为一种习惯。尤其是在市场波动加剧的时期，掌握实时、准确的价格信息，对于做出判断至关重要。今天，我们就来聚焦2026年的比特币市场，为大家提供一份详尽的今日价格查询指南，并解读背后的关键信息。\n一、2026年比特币今日核心行情速览\n在撰写本文时，我们综合了多家主流交易平台的数据。需要强调的是，比特币价格是实时变动的，不同平台之间可能存在微小价差，这属于正常现象。\n为了方便大家快速了解，我们将关键数据整理如下：\n计价货币 价格（约） 24小时涨跌幅\n美元 (USD) $85,430 +2.3%\n人民币 (CNY) ¥615,000 +2.1%\n交易量（24h） 约$420亿美元\n市值排名 全球数字资产第1位\n（注：以上为模拟数据，实际价格请以实时行情为准）\n从数据可以看出，当前比特币价格在经历了一段时间的盘整后，呈现出温和上涨的态势。这种走势往往与宏观市场情绪、监管动态以及大型机构的资金流向密切相关。\n二、如何正确查看与理解K线走势图\n“比特币价格今日行情k线图”是技术分析爱好者的核心工具。一张K线图蕴含了开盘价、收盘价、最高价和最低价四大关键信息。对于新手而言，看懂K线图是第一步。\n个人观点： 我认为，普通投资者不必沉迷于复杂的K线形态分析，但掌握几个基础概念非常有益。例如， 长长的下影线通常意味着在低价位有强劲的买盘支撑，而连续几根实体阳线则可能预示着上涨趋势的延续。\n以下是一些常见的K线图观察要点：\n趋势判断： 连接一段时间内的低点或高点，可以画出趋势线，直观判断市场处于上升、下降还是横盘通道。\n关键价位： 关注历史上的重要高点和低点，这些位置常成为价格的心理阻力位或支撑位。\n成交量配合： 价格上涨时如果伴随成交量放大，通常意味着趋势更健康、更可持续。\n三、美元与人民币计价差异的常见问题\n很多用户会同时搜索“比特币今日价格美元”和“比特币今日价格人民币”，并发现两者换算后不完全一致。这背后主要有两个原因：\nQ：为什么美元价和人民币换算价不同？\nA：这主要受两个因素影响：\n1.汇率波动： 人民币对美元的汇率是实时变动的，平台显示的人民币价格是基于实时汇率计算的结果。\n2.市场流动性差异： 不同国家或地区的交易市场供需关系不同，可能导致价格存在细微的“溢价”或“折价”。\nQ：我应该参考哪个价格？\nA：这取决于你的交易场景。\n如果你在国际交易所（如Binance、Coinbase）交易，通常以美元（USDT/USDC）计价为主要参考。\n如果你在国内背景的交易所或OTC平台进行法币交易，则应直接关注人民币计价的行情。\n操作建议： 对于长期持有者，关注美元计价的大趋势更为重要；对于频繁进行法币兑换交易的投资者，则需紧盯人民币价格及平台本身的买卖差价。\n四、获取实时行情的可靠方法与步骤\n依赖单一来源查询价格可能存在风险。我推荐一个多步骤的验证方法，以确保信息的准确性：\n选择主流信息聚合平台： 可以访问像 CoinMarketCap 或 CoinGecko 这样的全球性数据聚合网站。它们汇总了全球数百家交易所的价格，提供加权平均价，相对公允。\n核对头部交易所价格： 接着，去你常用的或全球顶级的几家交易所（如Binance, Kraken, Coinbase）官网查看实时报价。比较它们与聚合平台的价格是否在合理误差范围内。\n关注交易深度： 在交易所界面，不要只看最新成交价，还要观察买卖盘挂单（订单簿）的深度。深厚的买卖盘意味着市场流动性好，大额交易不易造成价格剧烈滑动。\n设置价格预警： 利用交易所或金融APP的价格提醒功能，为你关心的价位设置警报，这样就不必24小时盯盘，也能抓住关键时机。\n市场永远在变化，今天的价格只是漫长旅程中的一个瞬间坐标。理解价格背后的逻辑——无论是宏观经济的风吹草动，还是区块链技术本身的迭代升级——远比追逐短时的数字波动更有价值。保持学习，理性判断，才是应对这个充满活力又变幻莫测的市场的长久之道。\n2026年 走势 行情 人民币 美元\n","publishTime":"2026-05-16T16:33:00+08:00"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779087236283}}
{"type":"message","id":"5d2565e8","parentId":"9fe03f69","timestamp":"2026-05-18T06:53:56.286Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_f7c92a92c33f4b919a949224","toolName":"coze_web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Coze web search: Shanghai composite index today May 18 2026\n\nResults (10)\n1. 上证综合指数 (000001.SH)\n   URL: https://finance.sina.com.cn/realstock/company/sh000001/nc.shtml\n   Source: 新浪财经\n   Published: 2026-05-15T15:30:00+08:00\n   上证综合指数 (000001.SH)\n-42.53\n-1.02%\n4135.39\n停牌\n2026-05-15 15:30:39\n今 开：4174.18 最 高：4191.81\n昨 收：4177.92 最 低：4114.09\n成交量：7.33亿手 振 幅：1.86%\n成交额：15192.40亿元\n2026/05/15/五15:00 价 4135.39 均 4153.43 量 620.50万 幅 -1\n2. Major stock market indices worldwide\n   URL: http://www.china.org.cn/world/Off_the_Wire/2026-05/08/content_118482695.shtml\n   Source: China.org.cn\n   Published: 2026-05-08T00:00:00+08:00\n   jor stock markets worldwide on Friday.\nIN ASIA\nThe Shanghai Composite Index opened at 4,163.85 points,\nwn 266.49 points, or 1.00 percent.\nThe S&P/ASX 200 index opened at 8,729.40 points, down 148.70 points\n3. Chinese shares open higher Tuesday\n   URL: http://www.china.org.cn/china/Off_the_Wire/2026-05/12/content_118489351.shtml\n   Source: China.org.cn\n   Published: 2026-05-12T00:00:00+08:00\n   \n2026-05-12\nBEIJING, May 12 (Xinhua) -- Chinese stocks opened higher on Tuesday, with the benchmark Shanghai Composite Index up 0.10 percent to open at 4,229.28 points.\nThe Shenzhen Component Index op\n4. China - Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index\n   URL: https://en.macromicro.me/series/1071/cn-shanghai-stock-exchange-composite-index\n   Source: MacroMicro\n   Published: 2025-06-26T06:31:32+08:00\n   China - Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index\n3,455.97\n35.41\nLatest Stats\nChina - Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index\n3,455.97\n3,420.57\nSpecs\nCategory\nStock Market\nRegion\nChina\nFrequency\nDay\nUni\n5. China's Shanghai Composite Index opens up 0.3% to 4,256.16\n   URL: https://www.ainvest.com/news/china-shanghai-composite-index-opens-0-3-4-256-16-2605/\n   Source: AInvest\n   Published: 2026-05-13T21:30:00+08:00\n   \nBy Ainvest\nWednesday, May 13, 2026 9:30 pm ET\nThe Shanghai Composite Index opened higher on May 13, 2\nf the Trump–Xi summit scheduled for May 14–15. The index has gained 5.36% over the past month and is u\n6. Mainland stock market hits 11-year high\n   URL: http://en.people.cn/n3/2026/0512/c90000-20455108.html\n   Source: People's Daily Online\n   Published: 2026-05-12T00:00:00+08:00\n   Mainland stock market hits 11-year high\nBy Shi Jing in Shanghai (China Daily ) 08:38, May 12, 2026\nThe Shanghai Composite Index is displayed on a mobile phone. CHINA DAILY\nThe bullish momentum recentl\n7. Realtime News\n   URL: https://www.kgi.com.hk/en/market-news-and-analysis/market-news/market-news-feed?id=6028297&iid=6c7889a28a4d4e238aae64f447146057&type=scnews\n   Source: 凱基亞洲\n   Published: 2026-05-13T15:02:00+08:00\n   x closes at 4,242.57, up 0.67%\n(Infocast News) The Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index closed at 4\n,242.57 today, up 0.67%.\nData Source：INF\n\n8. The Shangai Composite Index Closes 0.69% Higher\n   URL: https://tradingeconomics.com/china/stock-market/news/550265\n   Source: TRADING ECONOMICS\n   Published: 2026-05-13T07:16:00+08:00\n   oints or 0.69 percent on Wednesday to close at 4244 points.\nGains were led by Datang Intl (10.00%), Shanghai Electric (7.77%) and Avic Aviation Engine (5.89%).\nBiggest losers were China Pacific Insu (\n9. Chinese shares open lower Friday\n   URL: https://www.chinadailyhk.com/hk/article/633179\n   Source: China Daily\n   Published: 2026-05-08T10:21:00+08:00\n   res open lower Friday\nBy Xinhua\nBEIJING - Chinese stocks opened lower on Friday, with the benchmark Shanghai Composite Index down 0.39 percent to open at 4,163.85 points.\nThe Shenzhen Component Index \n10. 盘后速递丨两市低开高走，创业板指突破4000点\n   URL: http://m.toutiao.com/group/7639313923652567579/?upstream_biz=VolcEngine\n   Source: 今日头条\n   Published: 2026-05-13T18:02:32+08:00\n   每日观点 ➤ 今日沪深三大指数低开高走，沪指收涨0.67%，创2015年7月以来新高；创业板指涨2.63%，突破4000点。两市成交较昨日小幅缩量至3.26万亿。美国4月通胀升温，核心指标超预期，从结构上看，能源价格继续走高与居住通胀的补偿性回升是主要推动项，地缘政治驱动的能源冲击与刚性住房成本叠加，正形成可能的滞胀风险。权益市场面临的核心再定价逻辑在于：降息叙事削弱后，依赖远期增长、廉价资金和稳 \n本文作者：博时基金"}],"details":{"query":"Shanghai composite index today May 18 2026","type":"web","count":10,"items":[{"title":"上证综合指数 (000001.SH)","url":"https://finance.sina.com.cn/realstock/company/sh000001/nc.shtml","siteName":"新浪财经","snippet":"上证综合指数 (000001.SH)\n-42.53\n-1.02%\n4135.39\n停牌\n2026-05-15 15:30:39\n今 开：4174.18 最 高：4191.81\n昨 收：4177.92 最 低：4114.09\n成交量：7.33亿手 振 幅：1.86%\n成交额：15192.40亿元\n2026/05/15/五15:00 价 4135.39 均 4153.43 量 620.50万 幅 -1","content":"上证综合指数 (000001.SH)\n-42.53\n-1.02%\n4135.39\n停牌\n2026-05-15 15:30:39\n今 开：4174.18 最 高：4191.81\n昨 收：4177.92 最 低：4114.09\n成交量：7.33亿手 振 幅：1.86%\n成交额：15192.40亿元\n2026/05/15/五15:00 价 4135.39 均 4153.43 量 620.50万 幅 -1.02%\n▲ ▼\n成交\nVOL: 6204974.00\nMA10: 2943087.00\n▲ ▼\n量比\nLB: 61.35\n▲ ▼\n","publishTime":"2026-05-15T15:30:00+08:00"},{"title":"Major stock market indices worldwide","url":"http://www.china.org.cn/world/Off_the_Wire/2026-05/08/content_118482695.shtml","siteName":"China.org.cn","snippet":"jor stock markets worldwide on Friday.\nIN ASIA\nThe Shanghai Composite Index opened at 4,163.85 points,\nwn 266.49 points, or 1.00 percent.\nThe S&P/ASX 200 index opened at 8,729.40 points, down 148.70 points","content":"Major stock market indices worldwide\nXinhua\nMay 8, 2026\n2026-05-08\nBEIJING, May 8 (Xinhua) -- The following are the indices of major stock markets worldwide on Friday.\nIN ASIA\nThe Shanghai Composite Index opened at 4,163.85 points, down 16.24 points, or 0.39 percent.\nThe Shenzhen Component Index opened at 15,520.38 points, down 121.51 points, or 0.78 percent.\nThe Hang Seng Index opened at 26,359.79 points, down 266.49 points, or 1.00 percent.\nThe S&P/ASX 200 index opened at 8,729.40 points, down 148.70 points, or 1.67 percent.\nThe 225-issue Nikkei Stock Average opened at 62,654.01 points, down 179.83 points, or 0.29 percent.\nThe Straits Times Index opened at 4,930.22 points, down 11.74 points, or 0.24 percent.\nThe Korea Composite Stock Price Index opened at 7,353.94 points, down 136.11 points, or 1.82 percent.\nIN THE UNITED STATES\nThe S&P 500 Index closed at 7,337.11 points, down 28.01 points, or 0.38 percent.\nThe Dow Jones Industrial Average closed at 49,596.97 points, down 313.62 points, or 0.63 percent.\nThe Nasdaq Composite Index closed at 25,806.20 points, down 32.74 points, or 0.13 percent.\nIN EUROPE\nThe DAX Index closed at 24,663.61 points, down 255.08 points, or 1.02 percent.\nThe FTSE 100 Index closed at 10,276.95 points, down 161.71 points, or 1.55 percent.\nThe Paris CAC 40 closed at 8,202.08 points, down 97.34 points, or 1.17 percent. Enditem\n","publishTime":"2026-05-08T00:00:00+08:00"},{"title":"Chinese shares open higher Tuesday","url":"http://www.china.org.cn/china/Off_the_Wire/2026-05/12/content_118489351.shtml","siteName":"China.org.cn","snippet":"\n2026-05-12\nBEIJING, May 12 (Xinhua) -- Chinese stocks opened higher on Tuesday, with the benchmark Shanghai Composite Index up 0.10 percent to open at 4,229.28 points.\nThe Shenzhen Component Index op","content":"Chinese shares open higher Tuesday\nXinhua\nMay 12, 2026\n2026-05-12\nBEIJING, May 12 (Xinhua) -- Chinese stocks opened higher on Tuesday, with the benchmark Shanghai Composite Index up 0.10 percent to open at 4,229.28 points.\nThe Shenzhen Component Index opened 0.34 percent higher at 15,952.79 points. Enditem\n","publishTime":"2026-05-12T00:00:00+08:00"},{"title":"China - Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index","url":"https://en.macromicro.me/series/1071/cn-shanghai-stock-exchange-composite-index","siteName":"MacroMicro","snippet":"China - Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index\n3,455.97\n35.41\nLatest Stats\nChina - Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index\n3,455.97\n3,420.57\nSpecs\nCategory\nStock Market\nRegion\nChina\nFrequency\nDay\nUni","content":"China - Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index\n3,455.97\n35.41\nLatest Stats\nChina - Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index\n3,455.97\n3,420.57\nSpecs\nCategory\nStock Market\nRegion\nChina\nFrequency\nDay\nUnits\nIndex\nSource\n[SSE]上海證券交易所\n","publishTime":"2025-06-26T06:31:32+08:00"},{"title":"China's Shanghai Composite Index opens up 0.3% to 4,256.16","url":"https://www.ainvest.com/news/china-shanghai-composite-index-opens-0-3-4-256-16-2605/","siteName":"AInvest","snippet":"\nBy Ainvest\nWednesday, May 13, 2026 9:30 pm ET\nThe Shanghai Composite Index opened higher on May 13, 2\nf the Trump–Xi summit scheduled for May 14–15. The index has gained 5.36% over the past month and is u","content":"China's Shanghai Composite Index opens up 0.3% to 4,256.16\nBy Ainvest\nWednesday, May 13, 2026 9:30 pm ET\nThe Shanghai Composite Index opened higher on May 13, 2026, rising 0.3% to 4,256.16, reflecting optimism ahead of the Trump–Xi summit scheduled for May 14–15. The index has gained 5.36% over the past month and is up 24.64% year-to-date, according to contract for difference (CFD) data. Investors are closely watching the high-stakes meeting, where trade relations are expected to dominate the agenda according to market analysis.\nTech stocks led the morning's gains, with Cambricon Technologies, Zhongji Innolight, and Victory Giant Technology rising by 3.05%, 3.07%, and 3.19%, respectively. Foxconn Industrial Internet and Suzhou TFC Optical Communication also posted strong performances, climbing 10% and 10.44%, respectively. In contrast, livestock and agriculture stocks such as Muyuan Foods and Wens Foodstuff Group declined amid expectations of progress on U.S.-China agricultural trade.\nThe index closed at 4,243 on Wednesday, up 0.67% from the previous session. Analysts project the Shanghai Composite to trade at 4,131.41 by the end of the quarter and 3,853.92 in 12 months according to forecasts .\n","publishTime":"2026-05-13T21:30:00+08:00"},{"title":"Mainland stock market hits 11-year high","url":"http://en.people.cn/n3/2026/0512/c90000-20455108.html","siteName":"People's Daily Online","snippet":"Mainland stock market hits 11-year high\nBy Shi Jing in Shanghai (China Daily ) 08:38, May 12, 2026\nThe Shanghai Composite Index is displayed on a mobile phone. CHINA DAILY\nThe bullish momentum recentl","content":"Mainland stock market hits 11-year high\nBy Shi Jing in Shanghai (China Daily ) 08:38, May 12, 2026\nThe Shanghai Composite Index is displayed on a mobile phone. CHINA DAILY\nThe bullish momentum recently seen in the Chinese market is likely to continue thanks to the structural opportunities provided by the country's rapid adoption of emerging technologies and ongoing economic recovery, said experts.\nTheir comments were made on Monday after the benchmark Shanghai Composite Index climbed to an 11-year high of 4225.02 points. The Shenzhen Component Index jumped 2.16 percent and the tech-heavy ChiNext in Shenzhen surged 3.5 percent. Combined trading value on the Shanghai, Shenzhen and Beijing bourses topped 3.56 trillion yuan ($520 billion), up nearly 16 percent from the previous trading day.\nA-share listed semiconductor firms fueled the Monday rally, reporting an average daily price gain of 5.01 percent.\nFang Jian, manager of the integrated circuit hybrid fund at Yinhua Fund, said the strong performance of Chinese tech companies may have just begun in earnest. The artificial intelligence surge and semiconductor localization will generate enormous investment opportunities in 2026 as chipmakers will see \"a big year of orders\".\nOn Friday, China's top internet, economic and industry regulators jointly issued a guideline to regulate the application and innovative development of AI agents.\nWhile foundational models remain the key investment thesis at the current stage, investors are recommended to keep a close eye on power suppliers, companies with deeper and earlier AI adoption, as well as AI enablers that benefit from China's semiconductor localization trend, experts from Morgan Stanley wrote in a report released on Sunday.\nThe development and application of new thematic indices, analysis tools driven by AI innovation and the completion of financial market infrastructure have fueled the Chinese capital market with robust momentum, said David Day, managing director of the London Stock Exchange Group for Asia-Pacific.\nChina's strong economic numbers over the past few months -including exports and industrial production — have provided more confidence to international investors, Thomas Fang, head of China Global Markets at UBS, said during a news briefing on Monday, adding that China is likely to reenter an inflationary cycle in the third quarter.\nMeng Lei, China equity strategist at UBS Securities, upgraded his forecast for A-share companies' profitability growth rate this year to 11 percent, up from 8 percent at the end of last year. This will serve as one major driver for an A-share bull run throughout 2026, Meng said.\nContinued capital inflows into the A-share market will be another engine, which will be comprised of household savings directed into wealth management products, recovery in the issuance of mutual fund products, thematic exchange traded funds and high net wealth individuals investing more in private equities or quantitative funds, he added.\nMarket sentiment was also buoyed on Monday as the Foreign Ministry announced that United States President Donald Trump will pay a three-day state visit to China from Wednesday.\nThe visit, which will take place as scheduled, will directly improve the risk appetite in the A-share market, said Chen Guo, chief strategist of Eastmoney Securities.\nOverall market confidence will be strengthened. Export companies may benefit in anticipation of a marginal easing in tariff tensions. In the event of phased procurement or investment arrangements, a potential sentiment-driven recovery may be seen in companies specializing in cyclical products, power equipment and machinery, Chen said.\n(Web editor: Zhong Wenxing, Liang Jun)\n","publishTime":"2026-05-12T00:00:00+08:00"},{"title":"Realtime News","url":"https://www.kgi.com.hk/en/market-news-and-analysis/market-news/market-news-feed?id=6028297&iid=6c7889a28a4d4e238aae64f447146057&type=scnews","siteName":"凱基亞洲","snippet":"x closes at 4,242.57, up 0.67%\n(Infocast News) The Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index closed at 4\n,242.57 today, up 0.67%.\nData Source：INF\n","content":"Realtime News\n2026.05.13 15:02\nChina News SSE Composite Index closes at 4,242.57, up 0.67%\n(Infocast News) The Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index closed at 4,242.57 today, up 0.67%.\nData Source：INF\n","publishTime":"2026-05-13T15:02:00+08:00"},{"title":"The Shangai Composite Index Closes 0.69% Higher","url":"https://tradingeconomics.com/china/stock-market/news/550265","siteName":"TRADING ECONOMICS","snippet":"oints or 0.69 percent on Wednesday to close at 4244 points.\nGains were led by Datang Intl (10.00%), Shanghai Electric (7.77%) and Avic Aviation Engine (5.89%).\nBiggest losers were China Pacific Insu (","content":"The Shangai Composite Index Closes 0.69% Higher\n2026-05-13 15:16\nBy TRADING ECONOMICS\nThe Shangai Composite Index gained 29 points or 0.69 percent on Wednesday to close at 4244 points.\nGains were led by Datang Intl (10.00%), Shanghai Electric (7.77%) and Avic Aviation Engine (5.89%).\nBiggest losers were China Pacific Insu (-4.06%), Fuyao Glass Indu (-3.89%) and ICBC (-3.21%).\nChina Shanghai Composite Stock Market Index\nChina\nStock Market\n","publishTime":"2026-05-13T07:16:00+08:00"},{"title":"Chinese shares open lower Friday","url":"https://www.chinadailyhk.com/hk/article/633179","siteName":"China Daily","snippet":"res open lower Friday\nBy Xinhua\nBEIJING - Chinese stocks opened lower on Friday, with the benchmark Shanghai Composite Index down 0.39 percent to open at 4,163.85 points.\nThe Shenzhen Component Index ","content":"Published: 10:21, May 8, 2026\nChinese shares open lower Friday\nBy Xinhua\nBEIJING - Chinese stocks opened lower on Friday, with the benchmark Shanghai Composite Index down 0.39 percent to open at 4,163.85 points.\nThe Shenzhen Component Index opened 0.78 percent lower at 15,520.38 points.\n","publishTime":"2026-05-08T10:21:00+08:00"},{"title":"盘后速递丨两市低开高走，创业板指突破4000点","url":"http://m.toutiao.com/group/7639313923652567579/?upstream_biz=VolcEngine","siteName":"今日头条","snippet":"每日观点 ➤ 今日沪深三大指数低开高走，沪指收涨0.67%，创2015年7月以来新高；创业板指涨2.63%，突破4000点。两市成交较昨日小幅缩量至3.26万亿。美国4月通胀升温，核心指标超预期，从结构上看，能源价格继续走高与居住通胀的补偿性回升是主要推动项，地缘政治驱动的能源冲击与刚性住房成本叠加，正形成可能的滞胀风险。权益市场面临的核心再定价逻辑在于：降息叙事削弱后，依赖远期增长、廉价资金和稳 \n本文作者：博时基金","content":"每日观点 ➤ 今日沪深三大指数低开高走，沪指收涨0.67%，创2015年7月以来新高；创业板指涨2.63%，突破4000点。两市成交较昨日小幅缩量至3.26万亿。美国4月通胀升温，核心指标超预期，从结构上看，能源价格继续走高与居住通胀的补偿性回升是主要推动项，地缘政治驱动的能源冲击与刚性住房成本叠加，正形成可能的滞胀风险。权益市场面临的核心再定价逻辑在于：降息叙事削弱后，依赖远期增长、廉价资金和稳定流动性的高估值策略将面临压力，而高现金回报、强定价能力的防御性板块或在相对意义上获得配置资金的倾向性回流。后续需继续关注美国公布的5月CPI数据，以验证本轮通胀抬升是阶段性脉冲还是趋势性上行。 消息面 ➤ 美国4月CPI同比上涨3.8%创近三年新高当地时间5月12日，美国劳工统计局数据显示，4月CPI经季调后环比上涨0.6%；未经季调同比上涨3.8%，高于市场预期的3.7%，创2023年5月以来新高。剔除食品和能源的核心CPI同比上涨2.8%，高于预期的2.7%，也创下2025年9月以来新高；环比上涨0.4%。简评：4月通胀数据全面超预期，根源在于美伊冲突驱动的能源供应中断，汽油价格同比暴涨28.4%。叠加住房、外出住宿、机票等核心服务价格的联动上行，进一步加剧了物价上涨对居民实际购买力的侵蚀。通胀反弹使美联储面临严峻的双向困境，若美国通胀持续高企，可能推迟美联储降息窗口，并对海外流动性及成长板块估值构成边际压制，后续需保持关注。➤ 美国参议院确认凯文·沃什出任美联储理事当地时间5月12日，美国参议院以51票赞成、45票反对的投票结果，正式确认凯文·沃什出任美联储理事，任期14年。此次投票为他接任下一任美联储主席铺平了关键道路。随后参议院已启动其担任主席的确认程序，相关投票最快可能于5月13日完成。现任主席鲍威尔的任期将于5月15日结束。简评：沃什出任理事并即将接任主席，标志着美联储货币政策方向的重大调整。其“小央行”主张意味着货币政策可能从危机应对模式逐步回归常态化。但沃什上任之际正值美国通胀显著反弹至3.8%，在压力下推行去监管与缩表政策，难免面临现实考验。沃什的政策取向及与行政部门的实际关系，或将影响后续美元流动性和全球资金配置预期，中长期需持续观察沃什上任后的实际操作。➤ 特朗普启程访华，黄仁勋临时登上“空军一号”随行5月13日，美国总统特朗普登上“空军一号”启程前往中国进行国事访问。英伟达CEO黄仁勋在初始名单未包含其名之后，于最后一刻登上专机加入随行代表团。此外随行商界领袖名单涵盖特斯拉CEO马斯克、苹果CEO库克，以及高通、美光、高盛、花旗、波音等企业负责人。简评：黄仁勋从“缺席”到“最后登机”的关键转折，折射出美方在半导体制裁与商业利益间的权衡。作为受对华出口限制影响最大的企业之一，黄仁勋先前多次呼吁政界放松出口管制，此次随行既释放了美方在AI芯片 \n本文作者：博时基金","publishTime":"2026-05-13T18:02:32+08:00"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779087236284}}
{"type":"message","id":"a51815df","parentId":"5d2565e8","timestamp":"2026-05-18T06:54:21.136Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Key findings from the search:\n\n1. **A50 futures**: Dropped over 1%, currently at 15,536 (down from 15,675). This is a significant move - the position's estimated current price would be around 104.53 (15,536/14,834 * 100), still in profit but reduced.\n\n2. **BTC**: Major crash! Dropped nearly 2.2% to $76,551 at one point (from $81,000), now around $77,000. Broke 78,000 and 77,000 levels. Over 108,000 liquidations totaling $656M. Driven by US-Iran conflict macro risks.\n   \n3. **Shanghai Composite**: Closed Friday at 4,135 (down 1.02% from 4,178), though it had hit 4,200+ earlier in the week. The A50 position is still profitable at around +4.53% with a new estimated price of 104.53, staying well above the 95 stop loss, though the profit has narrowed from yesterday's +5.67%. The 12:00 noon scan wasn't completed, so I need to document this market shift.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"重大变化！A50 跌超 1%，BTC 暴跌至 $76,551。补生成午盘报告。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3ed7e46b026145c89bd8408d","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# 午盘扫描报告\n\n**日期:** 2026-05-18（周一）  \n**扫描时间:** 14:53 CST（补 12:00 扫描）  \n**账户:** 高风险高收益模拟账户\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ 重大市场变化\n\n### 🇨🇳 A50 期货 — 跌超 1%\n- **昨收:** 15,675\n- **当前:** ~15,536（日内跌超 1%）\n- **开盘:** 跌 0.03%，盘中扩大至跌超 1%\n- **触发因素:** 美股上周五创新高后获利回吐、A股短线调整\n\n### ₿ BTC — 暴跌至 $76,551！\n- **昨价:** ~$81,000\n- **盘中低点:** $76,551（跌 2.2%，5月1日以来最低）\n- **当前:** ~$77,000\n- **爆仓:** 24小时 108,457 人爆仓，总额 $6.56 亿\n- **触发因素:** 美伊冲突引发宏观风险，全球债券抛售推高利率，通胀回升压制降息预期\n\n---\n\n## 📊 持仓更新\n\n### A50 多头\n\n| 项目 | 昨日 | 今日午盘 | 变化 |\n|------|------|----------|------|\n| 指数价格 | 15,675 | ~15,536 | -0.89% |\n| 持仓估价 | 105.67 | ~104.71 | -0.96% |\n| 浮动盈亏 | +141.75 | +117.75 | -24.00 |\n| 盈利率 | +5.67% | +4.71% | -0.96% |\n\n**缠论结构：**\n- 日线：上涨走势仍在，但今日回调触及 30 分钟中枢下沿（15,500）\n- **关键观察：** 若 15,500 支撑有