duled for May 14–15. The index has gained 5.36% over the pa\nference (CFD) data. Investors are closely watching the high-stakes m\n10. Realtime News\n   URL: https://www.kgi.com.hk/en/market-news-and-analysis/market-news/market-news-feed?id=6026571&iid=6c7889a28a4d4e238aae64f447146057&type=scnews\n   Source: 凱基亞洲\n   Published: 2026-05-11T15:02:00+08:00\n   .02, up 1.08%\n(Infocast News) The Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite \nIndex closed at 4,225.02 today, up 1.08%.\nData Source：INF\n"}],"details":{"query":"Shanghai composite index close today May 18 2026","type":"web","count":10,"items":[{"title":"Chinese shares close lower Monday","url":"http://www.china.org.cn/china/Off_the_Wire/2026-05/18/content_118499985.shtml","siteName":"China.org.cn","snippet":"6-05-18\nBEIJING, May 18 (Xinhua) -- Chinese stocks closed lower on Monday, with the benchmark Shanghai\n Composite Index down 0.09 percent to 4,131.53 points.\nThe Shenzhen Component Index closed 0.20 percen","content":"Chinese shares close lower Monday\nXinhua\nMay 18, 2026\n2026-05-18\nBEIJING, May 18 (Xinhua) -- Chinese stocks closed lower on Monday, with the benchmark Shanghai Composite Index down 0.09 percent to 4,131.53 points.\nThe Shenzhen Component Index closed 0.20 percent lower at 15,530.23 points. Enditem\n","publishTime":"2026-05-18T00:00:00+08:00"},{"title":"1st LD-Writethru: Chinese shares close lower Monday","url":"http://www.china.org.cn/china/Off_the_Wire/2026-05/18/content_118500126.shtml","siteName":"China.org.cn","snippet":"6-05-18\nBEIJING, May 18 (Xinhua) -- Chinese stocks closed lower on Monday, with the benchmark Shanghai\n Composite Index down 0.09 percent to 4,131.53 points.\nThe Shenzhen Component Index closed 0.20 percen","content":"1st LD-Writethru: Chinese shares close lower Monday\nXinhua\n| May 18, 2026\n2026-05-18\nBEIJING, May 18 (Xinhua) -- Chinese stocks closed lower on Monday, with the benchmark Shanghai Composite Index down 0.09 percent to 4,131.53 points.\nThe Shenzhen Component Index closed 0.20 percent lower at 15,530.23 points.\nThe combined turnover of these two indices totaled 2.89 trillion yuan (about 422.3 billion U.S. dollars), down 450.5 billion yuan from the previous trading day.\nOil and gas, memory chip and robot sectors led the gains, while those related to sports led the losses.\nThe ChiNext Index, tracking China's Nasdaq-style board of growth enterprises, lost 0.36 percent to close at 3,914.88 points.\nThe STAR Composite Index, which reflects the performance of stocks on China's sci-tech innovation board, closed 0.95 percent higher at 2,094.47 points. Enditem\n","publishTime":"2026-05-18T00:00:00+08:00"},{"title":"上证综合指数 (000001.SH)","url":"https://finance.sina.com.cn/realstock/company/sh000001/nc.shtml","siteName":"新浪财经","snippet":"上证综合指数 (000001.SH)\n-9.04\n-0.22%\n4126.35\n停牌\n2026-05-18 11:35:54\n今 开：4120.14 最 高：4145.66\n昨 收：4135.39 最 低：4110.83\n成交量：4.10亿手 振 幅：0.84%\n成交额：8748.51亿元\n2026/05/18/一11:30 价 4126.35 均 4130.38 量 158.47万 幅 -0.2","content":"上证综合指数 (000001.SH)\n-9.04\n-0.22%\n4126.35\n停牌\n2026-05-18 11:35:54\n今 开：4120.14 最 高：4145.66\n昨 收：4135.39 最 低：4110.83\n成交量：4.10亿手 振 幅：0.84%\n成交额：8748.51亿元\n2026/05/18/一11:30 价 4126.35 均 4130.38 量 158.47万 幅 -0.22%\n▲ ▼\n成交\nVOL: 1584698.00\nMA10: 1477463.80\n▲ ▼\n量比\nLB: 67.73\n▲ ▼\n","publishTime":"2026-05-18T11:35:00+08:00"},{"title":"A-Share Three Major Indices Slip 0.2%-0.5% at Midday; SEMIGHT INSTRUMENTS (688808.SH) Surges Over 11% to Vie for \"New Stock King\"","url":"http://www.aastocks.com/en/stocks/analysis/china-hot-topic-content.aspx?id=NOW.1524970&source=AAFN","siteName":"阿思達克財經網（AASTOCKS）","snippet":"idday, closing the half-day down 0.2% to 0.5%.\nThe Shanghai Composite Index closed at 4,126 at midday,\n down 9 points or 0.2%, with turnover of RMB874.851 billion. The Shenzhen Component Index fell 48 poin","content":"A-Share Three Major Indices Slip 0.2%-0.5% at Midday; SEMIGHT INSTRUMENTS (688808.SH) Surges Over 11% to Vie for \"New Stock King\"\naacat by AASTOCKS\n2026/05/18 11:50 CST\nSHORT SELL  STOCK INFO\nKey economic data for China\u0019s three growth drivers all missed expectations. Fixed Asset Investment for the first four months fell 1.6% YoY, versus expectations for a 1.7% increase. Added Value of Industries Above Designated Scale rose 4.1% YoY in April, below the expected 6% growth. April retail sales increased 0.2% YoY, missing the expected 2% rise. The RMB central parity against the USD was set at 6.8435, down 20 bps MoM. Today (18th), the PBOC conducted RMB1 billion seven-day reverse repo operations in the open market at an unchanged rate of 1.4%. With RMB1 billion maturing, there was zero net injection or withdrawal for the day. The three major A-share indices opened 0.4% to 0.9% lower, briefly turned positive, but reversed again before midday, closing the half-day down 0.2% to 0.5%.\nThe Shanghai Composite Index closed at 4,126 at midday, down 9 points or 0.2%, with turnover of RMB874.851 billion. The Shenzhen Component Index fell 48 points or 0.3% to 15,513, with turnover of RMB1.05 trillion. The ChiNext Index dropped 19 points or 0.5% to 3,909, with turnover of RMB504.716 billion.\nAmong financials, ICBC (601398.SH)  -0.050 (-0.691%)   and CCB (601939.SH)  -0.060 (-0.611%)   each slipped 0.3%. CHINA PACIFIC INSURANCE (601601.SH)  -0.670 (-1.940%)   declined 2.2%. BYD Company (002594.SZ)  -1.790 (-1.859%)   fell 1.7%. CONTEMPORARY AMPEREX (300750.SZ)  -6.370 (-1.504%)   dropped 1.7% after announcing cooperation with Xiamen to establish a regional production base for high-performance automotive and energy storage lithium batteries, and to strengthen collaboration in the low-altitude sector.\nOn its 25th trading day since listing, SEMIGHT INSTRUMENTS (688808.SH)  +174.990 (+14.956%)   sought to become the A-share \"New Stock King\". The stock once soared to RMB1,361 and closed the half-day up 11.5% at RMB1,304.6, with turnover of RMB3.53 billion and a total market capitalization of RMB133.939 billion. Incumbent \"Stock King\" KWEICHOW MOUTAI (600519.SH)  -9.950 (-0.746%)   slipped 0.6% to RMB1,325.02 at midday, with turnover of RMB3.934 billion and a market capitalization of RMB1.66 trillion.\nIn the chip sector, SMIC (688981.SH)  -1.400 (-1.176%)   fell nearly 1%, while HUA HONG (688347.SH)  -2.290 (-1.526%)   declined 1.1%. CAMBRICON (688256.SH)  +7.990 (+0.661%)   gained 1.6%. Domestic GPU makers METAX (688802.SH)  +13.120 (+1.834%)   and MOORE THREADS (688795.SH)  +32.240 (+4.853%)   rose 2.1% and 5.8%, respectively, after the unveiling of a National AI Application Pilot Base (Embodied Intelligence), where 18 leading companies including Unitree, METAX and MOORE THREADS formed a full industry chain alliance. LQKJ (688008.SH)  +0.010 (+0.004%)   edged up 0.6%. YANGTZE OPTICAL FIBRE (601869.SH)  +25.030 (+6.684%)   surged 5.5%.\nLeading domestic DRAM maker Changxin Technology is accelerating its IPO push. According to the Shanghai Stock Exchange website, Changxin Technology has completed updates to its financial reports and renewed its STAR Market IPO prospectus (filing draft), with the review status restored to \"Accepted\". Memory chip stock GIGADEVICE (603986.SH)  +24.660 (+6.570%)   jumped 7.3%. The updated prospectus shows that GIGADEVICE holds a 1.8% stake in Changxin Technology, and its chairman Zhu Yiming also serves as chairman of Changxin Technology.\nA Shares quote is delayed for at least 15 mins\n","publishTime":"2026-05-18T11:50:00+08:00"},{"title":"2026年5月18日（下周一）操作观察","url":"https://caifuhao.eastmoney.com/news/20260517192214704086760","siteName":"财富号","snippet":"2026年5月18日（下周一）操作观察\n股友衣常  2026年05月17日 19:22  上海\n周五主要指数集体调整，上证指数收盘报4135.39点，下跌1.02%；深证成指收盘报15561.37点，下跌1.17%；创业板指报3929.06点，下跌0.56%；科创50指数收盘1696.26点，下跌1.67%。成交方面，沪深两市全日成交额达3.34万亿元，与周四基本持平，量能保持稳定。不包括ST股，","content":"2026年5月18日（下周一）操作观察\n股友衣常  2026年05月17日 19:22  上海\n周五主要指数集体调整，上证指数收盘报4135.39点，下跌1.02%；深证成指收盘报15561.37点，下跌1.17%；创业板指报3929.06点，下跌0.56%；科创50指数收盘1696.26点，下跌1.67%。成交方面，沪深两市全日成交额达3.34万亿元，与周四基本持平，量能保持稳定。不包括ST股，当日涨停54家、跌停15家；两市上涨1693家，下跌3404家，下跌家数显著多于上涨家数。\n下周一沪指预计波动区间为4175—4105点，预计当日早上低开后小幅惯性探底，随后逐步企稳，4105点左右支撑展开修复行情，站稳4132点后顺势走高，全天以震荡反弹为主，不再延续单边杀跌态势。尽管近期国内外利空消息较多（全球股市大跌、10年期美债收益率突破4.55%、美降息预期下降、加息预期上升、中东地缘冲突反复、油价高位运行至109美元、国内社融数据不及预期），但当前调整仍为上升途中的正常调整，牛市多急跌，属于日线级别调整，调整预计从5月中旬持续至5月月末为期1周多时间，股指将维持高位震荡，而非单边下杀；3.34万亿的成交量表现良好，既说明市场承接无问题，也体现多空平衡，市场仍将延续原有轨迹，调整过后震荡向上，6月上旬前创出新高新的概率较大。\n重点关注几个方向：一是科技主线，优先布局相对低位的半导体设备和材料分支，适合科技板块内部高低切换；二是煤化工板块，该板块因5月中东冲突缓和已调整较长时间，而油价高位运行将提升其业绩，且业绩有望在2季报中体现，具备轮动修复潜力；其它可以看看上周五已经发酵的无水氢氟酸板块，韩国厂商自本月起从中国采购无水氢氟酸，价格较年初上涨约40%，板块具备短期催化动能；算力网板块，周末最热板块。\n下周一操作核心是逢低抄底冲高减仓，若上午市场惯性下探至4105点附近，可分批抄底买入，布局方向优先科技主线及周末发酵板块，不盲目抄底非核心品种；若盘中出现冲高走势，包括半导体设备和材料、人形机器人等板块，可分批减仓兑现利润，落袋为安；前期涨幅过大的光芯片光模块板块不碰，其盈亏比、性价比均不高，避免高位站岗；仓位上仍以科技板块为主线，大部分仓位用于科技板块内部高低切换，同时适度关注煤化工、无水氢氟酸、算力网等低位或者题材发酵板块，大盘整体看连续两日放量回落已基本出清恐慌盘和获利盘，盘面做空动能明显减弱，短线风险释放到位，下周一优先看超跌修复反弹，操作上不恐慌不追高高抛低吸。\n$晶瑞电材(SZ300655)$ ：半导体材料，有无水氢氟酸（电子级）概念，现有2.2万吨电子级氢氟酸产能\n$网宿科技(SZ300017)$ ：算力网核心标的，涉及算力租赁、数据中心等业务\n$光环新网(SZ300383)$ ：算力网相关标的，聚焦数据中心及云计算业务\n青云科技：云计算及算力服务\n金煤科技：受益于油价高位运行，业绩有望在2季报体现\n诚志股份：受益于油价高位运行，业绩有望在2季报体现\n","publishTime":"2026-05-18T00:00:00+08:00"},{"title":"Global Times | Shanghai Composite breaks 4,200 points as AI supercycle lifts Asian markets","url":"https://english.sse.com.cn/news/newsrelease/voice/c/c_20260512_10818229.shtml","siteName":"SHANGHAI STOCK EXCHANGE","snippet":"o moved higher.\nAt the close, the Shanghai Composite Index was up 1.\n an intraday circuit breaker. The index closed up 4.32 percent at 7,\n822.24 points, its first close above the 7,800 threshold.\nThe core d","content":"Global Times | Shanghai Composite breaks 4,200 points as AI supercycle lifts Asian markets\n11 May 2026\nMajor stock indices in the Chinese mainland reached multi-year highs on Monday, fueled by the booming artificial intelligence (AI) and semiconductor sectors. Analysts attributed the rally to the ongoing AI supercycle, which has boosted the entire semiconductor, computing power and storage industrial chains, driven by improving profitability prospects and robust growth in domestic demand for AI computing power.\nThe Shanghai Composite Index topped 4,200 points, while the ChiNext Index surged past 3,900 points, the highest since June 16, 2015. The STAR Market 50 Index hit a fresh all-time intraday high.\nTransactions on the Shanghai and Shenzhen stock markets reached 3.54 trillion yuan ($520 billion), the fourth-highest level this year. Market turnover has remained above 3 trillion yuan for four consecutive trading days.\nThere was a strong rally in the semiconductor industrial chain. JCET Group closed at the daily limit and hit a new all-time high, with its market capitalization nearing 100 billion yuan. CSIC Special Gases surged by the 20 percent daily limit. The memory chip sector boomed, with Netac Technology and Puya Semiconductor both jumping by the 20 percent daily limit, and the liquid cooling server sector also moved higher.\nAt the close, the Shanghai Composite Index was up 1.08 percent, the Shenzhen Component Index was 2.16 percent higher, and the ChiNext Index was up 3.5 percent.\nThe AI supercycle also lifted broader Asian markets, with South Korean equities rallying to record levels amid a surge in chip heavyweights. SK Hynix surged more than 11.51 percent at the close, and Samsung Electronics rose 6.33 percent.\nThe KOSPI 200 Index soared more than 6 percent, triggering an intraday circuit breaker. The index closed up 4.32 percent at 7,822.24 points, its first close above the 7,800 threshold.\nThe core driver is AI computing power, which is starting to generate tangible revenue opportunities. For years, the AI industry was largely in a heavy investment cycle with uncertain commercial returns. Now many tech firms are rolling out monthly token subscriptions and direct computing power sales, attracting a growing number of paying users and suggesting rising commercial viability for this business model, Ma Jihua, a veteran tech analyst, told the Global Times on Monday.\nChina Securities Co said in a research note that domestic AI computing power is booming on both the supply and demand sides, and demand for computing power will keep rising. On the demand side, DeepSeek raised up to 50 billion yuan in its first financing round, mostly to expand its AI computing resources. Doubao's daily token consumption doubled, jumping from 60 trillion at the end of last year to 120 trillion in early April, Yicai reported.\nDomestic chip supply is also expanding and being more widely used. IDC data showed that local chips took up 41 percent of China's cloud AI accelerator shipments in 2025, with Huawei ranking first in shipment volume, according to the research note.\nCITIC Securities noted that the explosive surge in demand for AI computing power has driven strong exports of products across the semiconductor industrial chain, making this category the biggest contributor to China's export growth in April, according to Yicai.\nIn AI computing power, chips and storage, China and South Korea boast distinct strengths. China leverages its robust large‑language model research and development, world‑leading AI application rollout and vast domestic demand. South Korea excels in high‑end storage, semiconductor manufacturing and R&D, with deep China‑based R&D and production integration, Ma said.\nThe two nations are highly complementary. South Korea leads in hardware and manufacturing, China in application ecosystems and market scale. Both can deepen cooperation in software‑hardware integration, capacity alignment and market sharing, to capture dividends from the AI supercycle, Ma added.\nhttps://www.globaltimes.cn/page/202605/1360710.shtml\n","publishTime":"2026-05-12T00:00:00+08:00"},{"title":"The Shangai Composite Index Closes 0.69% Higher","url":"https://tradingeconomics.com/china/stock-market/news/550265","siteName":"TRADING ECONOMICS","snippet":"x gained 29 points or 0.69 percent on Wednesday to close at 4244 points.\nGains were led by Datang Intl\n (10.00%), Shanghai Electric (7.77%) and Avic Aviation Engine (5.89%).\nBiggest losers were China Pacif","content":"The Shangai Composite Index Closes 0.69% Higher\n2026-05-13 15:16\nBy TRADING ECONOMICS\nThe Shangai Composite Index gained 29 points or 0.69 percent on Wednesday to close at 4244 points.\nGains were led by Datang Intl (10.00%), Shanghai Electric (7.77%) and Avic Aviation Engine (5.89%).\nBiggest losers were China Pacific Insu (-4.06%), Fuyao Glass Indu (-3.89%) and ICBC (-3.21%).\nChina Shanghai Composite Stock Market Index\nChina\nStock Market\n","publishTime":"2026-05-13T07:16:00+08:00"},{"title":"China - Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index","url":"https://en.macromicro.me/series/1071/cn-shanghai-stock-exchange-composite-index","siteName":"MacroMicro","snippet":"China - Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index\n3,455.97\n35.41\nLatest Stats\nChina - Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index\n3,455.97\n3,420.57\nSpecs\nCategory\nStock Market\nRegion\nChina\nFrequency\nDay\nUni","content":"China - Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index\n3,455.97\n35.41\nLatest Stats\nChina - Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index\n3,455.97\n3,420.57\nSpecs\nCategory\nStock Market\nRegion\nChina\nFrequency\nDay\nUnits\nIndex\nSource\n[SSE]上海證券交易所\n","publishTime":"2025-06-26T06:31:32+08:00"},{"title":"China's Shanghai Composite Index opens up 0.3% to 4,256.16","url":"https://www.ainvest.com/news/china-shanghai-composite-index-opens-0-3-4-256-16-2605/","siteName":"AInvest","snippet":"sday, May 13, 2026 9:30 pm ET\nThe Shanghai Composite Index opened hi\nmmit scheduled for May 14–15. The index has gained 5.36% over the pa\nference (CFD) data. Investors are closely watching the high-stakes m","content":"China's Shanghai Composite Index opens up 0.3% to 4,256.16\nBy Ainvest\nWednesday, May 13, 2026 9:30 pm ET\nThe Shanghai Composite Index opened higher on May 13, 2026, rising 0.3% to 4,256.16, reflecting optimism ahead of the Trump–Xi summit scheduled for May 14–15. The index has gained 5.36% over the past month and is up 24.64% year-to-date, according to contract for difference (CFD) data. Investors are closely watching the high-stakes meeting, where trade relations are expected to dominate the agenda according to market analysis.\nTech stocks led the morning's gains, with Cambricon Technologies, Zhongji Innolight, and Victory Giant Technology rising by 3.05%, 3.07%, and 3.19%, respectively. Foxconn Industrial Internet and Suzhou TFC Optical Communication also posted strong performances, climbing 10% and 10.44%, respectively. In contrast, livestock and agriculture stocks such as Muyuan Foods and Wens Foodstuff Group declined amid expectations of progress on U.S.-China agricultural trade.\nThe index closed at 4,243 on Wednesday, up 0.67% from the previous session. Analysts project the Shanghai Composite to trade at 4,131.41 by the end of the quarter and 3,853.92 in 12 months according to forecasts .\n","publishTime":"2026-05-13T21:30:00+08:00"},{"title":"Realtime News","url":"https://www.kgi.com.hk/en/market-news-and-analysis/market-news/market-news-feed?id=6026571&iid=6c7889a28a4d4e238aae64f447146057&type=scnews","siteName":"凱基亞洲","snippet":".02, up 1.08%\n(Infocast News) The Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite \nIndex closed at 4,225.02 today, up 1.08%.\nData Source：INF\n","content":"Realtime News\n2026.05.11 15:02\nChina News SSE Composite Index closes at 4,225.02, up 1.08%\n(Infocast News) The Shanghai Stock Exchange Composite Index closed at 4,225.02 today, up 1.08%.\nData Source：INF\n","publishTime":"2026-05-11T15:02:00+08:00"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779101633894}}
